        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 85-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout his stay. He was discharged in a stable condition with an updated inhaler regimen and advised on self-management strategies. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
